      "content": "When advocating against new carbon emission standards, focus on the immediate economic impact on your local Ohio manufacturing base. Argue that the increased compliance costs will lead to higher operational expenses, potentially forcing price increases that harm consumers or leading to job cuts in the community. You could also suggest that stricter regulations risk driving manufacturing operations out of state to areas with less stringent rules, impacting local tax revenue. Finally, present data showing how the cost burden disproportionately affects small and mid-sized local enterprises compared to larger corporations.",
